  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3757",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to bind to Kcnc3, Kcna7, and Kcnf1, all of which are involved in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Kcnh2, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Dalfampridine influences potassium channel function. The high scores in the visible paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Dalfampridine and Kcnh2, supported by overlapping pathways involving delayed rectifier potassium channels. The evidence suggests that Dalfampridine may modulate Kcnh2 through its interaction with these channels, potentially affecting potassium homeostasis. The mechanism is supported by the shared involvement of these channels in the same biological process, and the consistent binding interactions across different target proteins imply a general effect on potassium channel activity. The relationship is further strengthened by the presence of overlapping pathways, which suggests a broader functional impact on potassium regulation.",
